{
 "id": "llm-from-scratch",
 "group": "Build from Scratch",
 "title": "Language Modeling from Scratch",
 "blurb": "Build a modern language model end to end, one exercise at a time: tokenizers and Transformer blocks, GPU kernels and parallelism, scaling laws, inference, evaluation, data pipelines and post-training with preferences and verifiable rewards. Each problem isolates one piece you would otherwise only see buried inside a large training codebase.",
 "prereq": "You should be comfortable with Python, NumPy and PyTorch and know how attention and a Transformer block work; the PyTorch and Triton study plans are good preparation for the kernel sections.",
 "next": "Continue with the Inference Engineering study plan for serving in more depth, or the reinforcement learning problems for the policy-gradient ideas behind RLHF and GRPO.",
